LMForge source provenance
=========================

LMForge incorporates source code and tests derived from Stanford University's
CS336 Spring 2025 Assignment 1: Basics.

The initial LMForge source snapshot was imported from commit
314d731892705ac8f9606198d73b0d5168e7b846 of the local assignment1-basics
repository. The imported snapshot also includes one non-behavioral correction:
the indentation of the `targets` parameter in
`cs336_basics/training/loss.py`.

The following course-only or local-development files were intentionally not
imported:

- `cs336_spring2025_assignment1_basics.pdf`
- `make_submission.sh`
- `cs336_basics/docs/superpowers/`
- the source repository's `.gitignore`

The original Stanford copyright and MIT license are preserved in `LICENSE`.
Stanford University does not endorse this derivative project.
